From: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] torizon: set fitconf_memory to the SKU memory overlay

The boot script used to pick the memory overlay out of boot_conf with
setexpr, which the U-Boot command whitelist of signed builds does not
allow. Set fitconf_memory to the conf-memory-<size>.dtbo part of the SKU
entry instead, and delete it for an unknown SKU, so the boot script only
has to append it. boot_conf keeps its value.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
---
 board/mediatek/lec_mtk_i1200/lec_mtk_i1200.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/board/mediatek/lec_mtk_i1200/lec_mtk_i1200.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/lec_mtk_i1200/lec_mtk_i1200.c
@@ -308,11 +308,16 @@
     uint32_t sku_id = (sku_id_4 << 4) | (sku_id_3 << 3) | (sku_id_2 << 2) | (sku_id_1 << 1) | sku_id_0;
 
     int i;
+    env_set("fitconf_memory", NULL);
     for (i = 0; i < sizeof(skus)/sizeof(struct sku_info); i++) {
         if (skus[i].sku_id == sku_id) {
 		printf("SKU:   %s\n", skus[i].sku_str);
 		snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "setenv boot_conf '%s'", skus[i].dtbo_file);
 		run_command(cmd, 0);
+		/* The memory overlay alone; the FIT image has no other SKU overlay. */
+		snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "%.*s",
+			 (int)strcspn(skus[i].dtbo_file, "#"), skus[i].dtbo_file);
+		env_set("fitconf_memory", cmd);
 		break;
         }
     }
